{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsQKzxni9TJQfTaKEY8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled R16F1 **FIX**: assigning a command's output to a variable in PowerShell lets it launch a model past the blackout hook. The verdict is committed as `55cab97b` in `docs/reviews/wi-834/017-ADJUDICATE-1003705.md`, with the `WI: WI-834` trailer.\n\n**What I reproduced:** I called `launch_reason`, the function the hook bases its denial on, against this repo's own `agents.toml`.\n- **Allowed (the defect):** `$response = claude -p x`, and the variants `[string]$r =`, `$a, $b =`, `$r +=` and `$env:X =`.\n- **Denied:** plain `claude -p x`, the forms `$r = (…)`, `$r = & …` and `$r = $(…)`, and Bash's `r=$(claude -p x)`.\n- **Correctly allowed:** quoted values such as `$r = 'claude -p x'`.\n\nThe cause is in `_segment_command`: it skips only POSIX `NAME=value` assignments, so it treats the PowerShell variable `$response` as the command. In a real PowerShell session, `$r = cmd /c echo …` and the typed and multi-variable forms all ran the right-hand command, while a quoted string stayed literal.\n\n**Why FIX:**\n- **In scope:** unlike the line-continuation trick I dismissed in sitting 005, this needs no contrived input. It is PowerShell's ordinary way to capture a command's output, the counterpart of the Bash form the hook already denies.\n- **A real gap:** it breaks the coverage LLR-300 and the spec promise, which is to deny any call that names a model CLI as a command word.\n- **Cheap:** the fix sits in the one shell-reading boundary, about 30 to 45 lines plus tests. Quoted values have to stay data so that `$r = 'claude'` is not falsely denied.\n\nThe builder also argued for FIX, and their account of the code held up. The row text already describes the intended behaviour, so no re-attestation should be needed unless its wording changes. My probe script is in the session scratchpad, not the repo, and the `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2609,"cache_read_input_tokens":454184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2609},"output_tokens":728,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"5ec5caea-17d1-49a2-b8a2-0948a4c5884c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T21:51:09.342Z","request_id":"req_011CfsQKzhfMUkeMiyC7rs1T"}
