owed (the defect):** `$response = claude -p x`, and the variants `[string]$r =`, `$a, $b =`, `$r +=` and `$env:X =`.\n- **Denied:** plain `claude -p x`, the forms `$r = (…)`, `$r = & …` and `$r = $(…)`, and Bash's `r=$(claude -p x)`.\n- **Correctly allowed:** quoted values such as `$r = 'claude -p x'`.\n\nThe cause is in `_segment_command`: it skips only POSIX `NAME=value` assignments, so it treats the PowerShell variable `$response` as the command. In a real PowerShell session, `$r = cmd /c echo …` and the typed and multi-variable forms all ran the right-hand command, while a quoted string stayed literal.\n\n**Why FIX:**\n- **In scope:** unlike the line-continuation trick I dismissed in sitting 005, this needs no contrived input. It is PowerShell's ordinary way to capture a command's output, the counterpart of the Bash form the hook already denies.\n- **A real gap:** it breaks the coverage LLR-300 and the spec promise, which is to deny any call that names a model CLI as a command word.\n- **Cheap:** the fix sits in the one shell-reading boundary, about 30 to 45 lines plus tests. Quoted values have to stay data so that `$r = 'claude'` is not falsely denied.\n\nThe builder also argued for FIX, and their account of the code held up. The row text already describes the intended behaviour, so no re-attestation should be needed unless its wording changes. My probe script is in the session scratchpad, not the repo, and the `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator.","ttft_ms":2678,"type":"result","duration_ms":84738,"uuid":"a07f2c71-654b-43bb-ac88-bc124ee5691c","ttft_stream_ms":1609,"time_to_request_ms":598,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":24,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":222,"input_hooks":292,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":8,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":9,"message_normalization":12,"client_creation":3,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":22,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":593,"time_to_request_major_faults":6070,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"nested_memory","slowest_producer_ms":176,"cpu_ms":329,"major_faults":2934,"changed_files_reread":7},"first_content_frame_ms":1609,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
